WEBVTT

00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:03.042
- Previously on The O.C.:
- Where's my brother?

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.833
- Trey's looking at three to five years.
- You like Seth Cohen!

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:08.625
I can't like Seth Cohen.
If you tell anyone, I'll kill you.

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:10.542
What have you two been doing?

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.708
Kiki tells me you've been in the office
alone together till 2 in the morning.

00:00:14.917 --> 00:00:18.292
Aren't they the perfect couple? They've
been keeping their romance a secret...

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.750
...but tonight, the secret's out.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:26.000
Mom, no recipes. Put them away.

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:28.417
This is Ryan's first Thanksgiving
in the house...

00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:31.000
...and we're gonna
make this meal as a family.

00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:33.500
- Seriously, where's Rosa?
- No Rosa. Just us.

00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:36.667
- I, for one, am ready for this challenge.
- Dad, takeout menus.

00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:39.208
- Sandy!
- You sure you wanna do this?

00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:41.917
Mom, no. No!
We're not ruining Thanksgiving!

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.333
- Who said we are?
- I wait for this event every year.

00:00:45.542 --> 00:00:47.833
Please!
Thanksgiving is my favorite holiday.

00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:50.625
- Everyone knows this.
- My family was never into holidays.

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:53.000
All the more reason to make this special.

00:00:53.208 --> 00:00:56.792
- Are there any pans anywhere?
- Not inspiring a lot of confidence, darling.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.417
Know what I dream about when I dream
about Thanksgiving, which is often?

00:01:00.625 --> 00:01:03.458
I dream about eating
so much deliciousness...

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:06.500
...that all the blood rushes
to my stomach and I pass out.

00:01:06.708 --> 00:01:09.458
- Please don't deny me that.
- That's just weird.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:12.625
Well, I guess we should start
with the turkey.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.167
Do I...?

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.375
That's just how she held you as a baby.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.125
Sandy.

00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:28.792
I guess we should just start basting?

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:32.917
- Tell you what, I'll baste.
- That's a good idea.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:36.083
- Are you sure?
- Oh, I love to baste, you know that.

00:01:36.292 --> 00:01:38.792
Okay. Well, next up is cranberries.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.958
- I got it. Big fan of the cranberry.
- Then I'll peel the potatoes.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:46.917
You know what? There's few things as
therapeutic as peeling a potato. I'm sorry.

00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:50.042
- So, what am I supposed to do?
- Set the table.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.208
Yeah. Setting the table's important.

00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:56.208
- How about I get the phone?
- Or you can answer the phone.

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:58.167
You own the phone.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:00.833
Hello?

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:05.083
Yeah, I'll accept the charges.

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.583
Yeah, he's right here.
Hold on a second.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.500
Ryan, it's your brother.

00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:20.292
I'm just gonna...

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:25.000
He's...
He's calling from jail.

00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:27.417
Well, he's gonna be there for a while.

00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:29.917
- Hey, did you ever meet him?
- No.

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:35.708
It's just that I've gotten used to Ryan
in the family. You forget he has his own.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.917
Hey, bro.

00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:43.167
Good. You?

00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:50.292
What, today? It's Thanksgiving, Trey.

00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:56.542
No. Yeah, I know.
It's been a long time. It's just...

00:03:00.375 --> 00:03:02.542
Wasn't Mom gonna see you?

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.958
Okay.

00:03:08.042 --> 00:03:10.167
No, I wanna see you too.

00:03:10.375 --> 00:03:13.500
It's been too long, so...

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.667
You too.

00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:19.083
Bye.

00:03:23.792 --> 00:03:25.042
How's Trey?

00:03:26.292 --> 00:03:28.792
Okay. He was hoping I could visit him.

00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:33.292
Holidays. He doesn't wanna be alone.

00:03:34.042 --> 00:03:35.292
Can you blame him?

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.042
So are you gonna go?

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.083
Well, it's only an hour away.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.458
I could help out here, go down,
be back by dinner.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.083
Great. That'll be great.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.250
You get to see your brother.

00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:27.250
People actually make stuffing?

00:04:27.458 --> 00:04:29.042
What did you think?

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.875
I didn't.

00:04:34.083 --> 00:04:36.625
So you should probably
be heading out soon.

00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:41.375
I gotta finish the stuffing.
Then there's the gravy and candied yams.

00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:45.542
And if you find enough cooking to last
three to five years, then Trey'll be out.

00:04:47.292 --> 00:04:50.125
He's just gonna want something
from me. A favor, money.

00:04:50.292 --> 00:04:52.667
Maybe not. Maybe he just wants
to see his family.

00:04:52.875 --> 00:04:55.542
- You don't know Trey.
- I know. You never talk about him.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.208
Not a lot to talk about.

00:04:58.417 --> 00:05:00.667
He's your brother.

00:05:00.875 --> 00:05:05.125
But if you want, I'll go with you.
I'd like to meet him.

00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:07.292
No, you wouldn't.

00:05:08.292 --> 00:05:11.292
Well, legally, Ryan,
we're all, like, brothers now, so...

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.542
Someone has to keep
your mom away from the food.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.125
Besides, you've got Anna coming over.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.875
Yes, I do.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:25.875
- You think Ryan's okay?
- I think he'll be okay.

00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:28.958
- He needs to do this.
- Okay.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:32.333
- Let me get in there, do some flipping.
- No. Seth really likes corn.

00:05:32.542 --> 00:05:35.292
- How do you expect me to get better?
- I don't!

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.708
- Sorry. The boys and I made a pact.
- A pact?

00:05:37.917 --> 00:05:39.667
- A solemn promise.
- When?

00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:43.042
You were in the bathroom.
I'm all for you expanding your horizons.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.167
But not today. We have guests, who
expect that food will actually be served.

00:05:47.375 --> 00:05:50.375
Speaking of which,
did you tell Rachel about Jimmy?

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:53.042
- No. Did you tell Jimmy about Rachel?
- No.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:57.083
He's freaked out enough.
First Thanksgiving without his wife.

00:05:57.292 --> 00:05:59.875
Well, I bet he'll have
less indigestion this year.

00:06:00.083 --> 00:06:02.750
Unlike your father,
who will probably be in agony.

00:06:02.958 --> 00:06:07.208
I can't believe he is having
Thanksgiving with Julie Cooper.

00:06:07.917 --> 00:06:11.792
- Because he's never had it with us.
- Well, no complaint here.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.583
Mom, you're uncomfortably close
to the corn right now.

00:06:14.792 --> 00:06:17.375
Can we just back up a little bit?

00:06:20.417 --> 00:06:22.458
I should have just gone to Grandma's.

00:06:22.667 --> 00:06:24.958
Because I really don't wanna go
to Mom's.

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:26.417
It's just for an hour.

00:06:26.625 --> 00:06:29.000
Why do we have to
spend Thanksgiving with him?

00:06:29.208 --> 00:06:31.125
He's creepy.

00:06:31.333 --> 00:06:34.167
Caleb's not creepy, he's just...

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.958
- Scary.
- He's dating Mom.

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:42.708
- I'm well aware.
- Well, isn't that weird for you?

00:06:42.917 --> 00:06:46.375
Look, your mom is... She's moving on.

00:06:46.583 --> 00:06:48.958
But I got news for you,
so's your dad.

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:51.000
Really?

00:06:51.208 --> 00:06:53.208
Well, not exactly.

00:06:53.417 --> 00:06:57.667
I mean, there's the fraud charges
and the whole bankruptcy thing.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:02.542
You know, I don't even have a job,
so I'm not exactly a catch, but...

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.208
Feel free to disagree.

00:07:05.417 --> 00:07:09.708
Look, I know it's weird, all right?
But your mom is still your mom.

00:07:10.917 --> 00:07:12.458
She loves you.

00:07:13.208 --> 00:07:14.375
Come on.

00:07:16.542 --> 00:07:18.833
- Better get on the road.
- Just one second.

00:07:19.042 --> 00:07:20.333
Trey doesn't even read comics.

00:07:20.542 --> 00:07:22.708
Not yet, but he hasn't seen
the new Titans.

00:07:22.917 --> 00:07:26.542
Titans. What about Legion?
That was kind of cooler.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.792
The guy's in prison, man.
Have you seen Oz? I'm sure that'll be fine.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.833
But, yeah, the new Legion is cooler.

00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:40.958
Hey! Hey!

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:43.667
Easy on my eau de toilette, please.

00:07:43.875 --> 00:07:46.125
Since when did you start
wearing cologne?

00:07:47.417 --> 00:07:50.792
I'm sorry for trying
to step it up a notch.

00:07:51.917 --> 00:07:55.833
- Since today.
- Oh, right, because Anna's coming over.

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:57.917
What?

00:07:58.125 --> 00:08:01.375
No. Why would you...?
Why would you even wear...?

00:08:01.583 --> 00:08:03.708
Anna? Are you totally...?

00:08:03.917 --> 00:08:06.667
I don't even... I don't. I couldn't. No.

00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:08.708
- You like her.
- What makes you think that?

00:08:08.917 --> 00:08:11.583
What's the problem?
She's cool. She's into you.

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.875
Okay, I need to ask your advice
on something...

00:08:16.083 --> 00:08:19.625
...but you have to promise me
that you will not tell anybody.

00:08:19.833 --> 00:08:21.125
- Promise?
- Promise.

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.792
The other night,
on my grandfather's yacht...

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.833
...Summer attacked me with her lips.

00:08:27.042 --> 00:08:29.500
And she swore if I told anyone,
she would kill me.

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:32.250
- She's got an interesting take on romance.
- Yeah.

00:08:32.458 --> 00:08:36.208
So the first 16 years of my life,
I have no women, now I have two.

00:08:36.417 --> 00:08:39.292
- Yeah, I feel really bad for you.
- Hey, thanks, buddy.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.542
Seriously, man, tough problem to have.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:45.125
I liked it so much better
when you had no sense of humor.

00:08:47.958 --> 00:08:50.875
- Happy Thanksgiving.
- Welcome.

00:08:51.083 --> 00:08:53.375
- Good to see you.
- How are you?

00:08:53.583 --> 00:08:56.417
- Happy Thanksgiving.
- You look very nice.

00:08:56.583 --> 00:09:00.250
Just wanted to stop by
before I went to my mom's.

00:09:00.458 --> 00:09:03.000
See if you wanted to talk.

00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:04.875
Your pool house or mine?

00:09:05.083 --> 00:09:09.292
- It's a twist-off, so that's classy.
- You've outdone yourself.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:13.333
- So Thanksgiving. Big day. Excited?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:09:13.542 --> 00:09:16.208
- New shirt?
- I guess.

00:09:16.375 --> 00:09:18.917
- Yeah, it's a tuck-in.
- Apparently.

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:21.625
And you wore your hair like... Like this.

00:09:21.833 --> 00:09:26.583
I... Yeah. I wasn't aware that...
Do I wear my hair any way?

00:09:26.792 --> 00:09:29.792
What's going on? It's just us, right?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.958
- Hey, I'm a fan of the tuck-in.
- And your hair looks good.

00:09:42.292 --> 00:09:45.583
- I gotta go. My mom's waiting.
- Okay.

00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:49.458
- I'll be back in, like, an hour.
- Great. I should be back by 8.

00:09:49.667 --> 00:09:52.083
- Where are you going?
- To see my brother.

00:09:52.292 --> 00:09:54.417
- I thought he was in...
- He is.

00:09:55.167 --> 00:09:58.292
But he called.
He wants me to drive down to visit him.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:02.042
- You want company?
- No, it's okay.

00:10:03.417 --> 00:10:05.333
You don't want to...

00:10:05.542 --> 00:10:09.375
No, I wanna see where you're from,
where you lived.

00:10:11.083 --> 00:10:12.542
You should be with your mom.

00:10:14.458 --> 00:10:17.125
You have this whole life
I don't know anything about.

00:10:17.292 --> 00:10:18.917
- It's better that way.
- No, it's not.

00:10:19.125 --> 00:10:20.667
Yes, it is.

00:10:23.542 --> 00:10:26.958
Look, it's...
It's not my life anymore.

00:10:28.083 --> 00:10:31.125
So, what does it matter, right?

00:10:45.667 --> 00:10:49.083
- Rachel!
- Hi! Happy Thanksgiving.

00:10:49.292 --> 00:10:52.583
- Happy Thanksgiving. Thank you.
- So sweet.

00:10:52.792 --> 00:10:54.375
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:10:54.583 --> 00:10:56.625
- Thanks for coming.
- Sure.

00:10:59.917 --> 00:11:01.542
Well!

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:06.083
So this is the summer cottage
for weekend getaways?

00:11:06.292 --> 00:11:09.125
That means "nice house" in Rachel.

00:11:12.875 --> 00:11:16.042
- Hey.
- Hi. I'm Jimmy. We met...

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:18.042
- Yeah, at La Roca.
- Right.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:22.958
Right. Great. Jimmy, Rachel.
Hey, why don't you both have a seat.

00:11:23.917 --> 00:11:25.625
Okay.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:39.125
Okay, well... I have to
check on something in the kitchen.

00:11:39.333 --> 00:11:41.042
As do I.

00:11:46.083 --> 00:11:48.917
- We suck!
- That was not very smooth.

00:11:49.083 --> 00:11:51.333
- I told you this was a bad idea.
- No, you didn't.

00:11:51.542 --> 00:11:53.708
I don't wanna know, don't care.

00:11:54.458 --> 00:11:56.833
Okay, so I'm gonna take off.

00:11:57.042 --> 00:11:58.208
Hey.

00:12:00.833 --> 00:12:03.042
Just in case, take this.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.208
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

00:12:05.417 --> 00:12:08.583
- Want anyone to go with you?
- No, I'm okay.

00:12:08.792 --> 00:12:11.083
Okay, well, you should take the keys.

00:12:11.292 --> 00:12:15.042
And I have a little something for Trey.

00:12:20.375 --> 00:12:23.458
- Don't worry, it's store-bought.
- Nice.

00:12:23.667 --> 00:12:25.792
- Later on, buddy.
- All right.

00:12:27.083 --> 00:12:29.958
What, too much? Hey, seriously.
Did I put too much on?

00:12:34.375 --> 00:12:36.500
Did you guys hear that Ryan's funny now?

00:12:49.083 --> 00:12:51.417
- What are you doing?
- I'm coming with you.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.875
My mom said it was okay.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:57.958
She did?

00:12:58.167 --> 00:13:02.208
Yeah, well, she's trying to
stay on my good side these days.

00:13:02.417 --> 00:13:04.750
I don't know.

00:13:04.958 --> 00:13:06.875
I do.

00:13:17.625 --> 00:13:19.250
Thanks.

00:14:07.875 --> 00:14:09.417
Hey, little brother.

00:14:09.625 --> 00:14:10.875
Hi.

00:14:11.667 --> 00:14:13.833
This is Marissa.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.333
Good to see you, man.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.667
You know what? You guys talk.

00:14:28.625 --> 00:14:31.167
I'll just be over here.

00:14:40.792 --> 00:14:42.792
Look at you, man.

00:14:43.708 --> 00:14:46.000
Sorry I haven't come by to see you.

00:14:46.208 --> 00:14:49.917
You've been busy. Mom said
you'd done pretty good for yourself.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.625
- How you been?
- You know. Not so good.

00:14:57.917 --> 00:14:59.833
- What do you need?
- Don't say it like that.

00:15:00.042 --> 00:15:02.500
- Can't a guy just see his brother?
- You tell me.

00:15:02.708 --> 00:15:04.583
Hey, forget about it, all right?

00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:13.833
I didn't wanna have to call you,
but I'm in trouble.

00:15:14.542 --> 00:15:17.667
When we got arrested,
I owed some people a lot of money.

00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:21.500
- Money that I lost, like, 6 grand.
- How'd you lose 6 grand?

00:15:21.708 --> 00:15:24.167
I'm an Atwood, bro. You know our luck.

00:15:25.292 --> 00:15:27.667
The people that I owe it to...

00:15:28.667 --> 00:15:31.667
...they got friends in here
who like to remind me about it.

00:15:32.542 --> 00:15:35.042
It's only gonna get worse.

00:15:36.208 --> 00:15:40.042
- I don't have that kind of money.
- I'm not asking you for the money.

00:15:41.292 --> 00:15:43.000
So, what are you asking me for?

00:15:46.875 --> 00:15:50.000
- You can't tell me where we're going?
- Bus station. You're going home.

00:15:50.208 --> 00:15:54.000
- What? Ryan...
- I have to pick up a stolen car, okay?

00:15:54.208 --> 00:15:57.500
That I have to drop off
at some chop shop to pay back a debt.

00:15:59.042 --> 00:16:01.333
- A stolen car.
- Now you know why you're not coming.

00:16:01.542 --> 00:16:04.208
- But if you get caught...
- He's my brother.

00:16:05.083 --> 00:16:06.875
If I don't do this...

00:16:08.083 --> 00:16:10.583
I've got no choice, okay?

00:16:11.708 --> 00:16:13.583
Me either.

00:16:13.792 --> 00:16:16.042
I'm not leaving you.

00:16:26.125 --> 00:16:28.625
Can you believe
Seth has a girl coming over?

00:16:28.833 --> 00:16:31.167
- I know!
- How can I help?

00:16:31.375 --> 00:16:33.833
- Hi.
- You must be Anna. Sandy Cohen.

00:16:34.042 --> 00:16:38.667
- Nice to meet you.
- We're doing fine, just working away.

00:16:38.875 --> 00:16:42.750
If by "we" you're referring to yourself,
then somebody violated the pact.

00:16:42.958 --> 00:16:45.333
I'm opening the wine,
a skill I feel confident about.

00:16:45.542 --> 00:16:48.500
- No argument here.
- So, Anna, what's the deal?

00:16:48.708 --> 00:16:52.500
Your parents don't believe in celebrating
the genocide of the American Indian?

00:16:52.708 --> 00:16:55.125
They went to Pittsburgh
to have dinner with the rest of the clan.

00:16:55.333 --> 00:16:58.250
- Oh, you didn't wanna go?
- No.

00:16:58.458 --> 00:17:03.875
It's kind of challenging to sit at a table
with the Sterns and still have an appetite.

00:17:04.083 --> 00:17:07.792
It's sort of an anathema
to the whole spirit of Thanksgiving.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.000
Anathema? Anathema.

00:17:13.458 --> 00:17:16.000
- Yes.
- Hey.

00:17:16.208 --> 00:17:19.958
Sweet potatoes and marshmallows and
cornflakes. Suddenly not so hungry.

00:17:20.167 --> 00:17:23.042
Well, then, all you'll be eating
are your words.

00:17:35.125 --> 00:17:37.458
Seth, a little help, please.

00:17:46.875 --> 00:17:49.000
You're trying to set me up
with Jimmy Cooper.

00:17:49.208 --> 00:17:51.125
- That's crazy.
- Yes, it is.

00:17:51.333 --> 00:17:53.458
- He's a white-collar criminal.
- But a nice one.

00:17:53.667 --> 00:17:58.083
How desperate do you think I am?
Don't answer that.

00:17:58.292 --> 00:18:00.458
- Look, Jimmy's a good guy.
- He's a thief.

00:18:00.667 --> 00:18:04.167
And you're a lawyer.
It's a perfect match.

00:18:05.875 --> 00:18:08.917
You don't wanna deal
with what's going on between us.

00:18:09.125 --> 00:18:13.000
There is nothing going on between us.
We're coworkers and friends. That's it.

00:18:13.208 --> 00:18:16.667
- Jimmy's cool, he's funny, he's attractive.
- It's not happening, Sandy.

00:18:20.208 --> 00:18:24.000
- Okay, admit it.
- Admit what?

00:18:24.208 --> 00:18:26.292
This whole thing is a setup.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:29.500
Should I use orange candles
or brown candles?

00:18:31.125 --> 00:18:33.167
Just say it.

00:18:45.917 --> 00:18:47.958
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:18:52.625 --> 00:18:55.375
I didn't know about the, you know...

00:18:55.542 --> 00:18:56.917
Oh, me neither.

00:18:57.083 --> 00:19:01.042
Okay, I just wanted to...
Wanted to make that clear.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:02.500
Good.

00:19:03.458 --> 00:19:05.542
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:09.500
- Oh, come on, break that tackle, baby.
- No, kill him. Kill him!

00:19:09.875 --> 00:19:14.750
- Hit him! Hit him!
- He could go all the way!

00:19:18.042 --> 00:19:19.417
Touchdown!

00:19:19.583 --> 00:19:22.125
- Dolphins fan.
- Huge. You're a Cowboys fan?

00:19:22.333 --> 00:19:23.875
Obsessed.

00:19:24.042 --> 00:19:26.000
- We've got a game here.
- Yeah, we do.

00:19:34.042 --> 00:19:35.417
- I don't want it.
- Why not?

00:19:35.583 --> 00:19:40.000
- It's two-week-old gravy.
- It's not, I just made it.

00:19:41.042 --> 00:19:43.875
Do you ever watch ESPN Classics?

00:19:44.042 --> 00:19:46.000
Oh, my God, I love ESPN Classics.

00:19:46.208 --> 00:19:48.625
There's something about it. It's so...

00:19:48.833 --> 00:19:52.000
...soothing.
- Soothing. Yes, it's totally soothing.

00:19:52.208 --> 00:19:54.250
I don't know what that is.

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.667
The gruesome twosome!

00:20:00.875 --> 00:20:03.833
That means "Happy Thanksgiving"
in Sandy.

00:20:04.042 --> 00:20:07.167
Our caterer's truck broke down
with our entire Thanksgiving feast.

00:20:07.375 --> 00:20:10.333
- I wanted to tell Marissa we're eating out.
- She's not here.

00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:14.375
Or we could just eat here.
You don't mind, do you, Kiki?

00:20:14.583 --> 00:20:18.292
- No. Why would I mind?
- Football's on, I forgot.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:22.708
- Cal, please, make yourself at home.
- Why not? It's mine.

00:20:24.125 --> 00:20:28.167
I don't understand. If Marissa's
not here, where is she? With Ryan?

00:20:28.375 --> 00:20:31.125
He went home. He left this morning.

00:20:33.083 --> 00:20:34.833
- Julie.
- Jimmy.

00:20:35.042 --> 00:20:36.792
Rachel.

00:20:38.917 --> 00:20:42.333
Rachel, Jimmy. What's the score?

00:21:00.208 --> 00:21:03.208
So this is your old neighborhood.

00:21:13.167 --> 00:21:15.250
Ryan Atwood.

00:21:15.458 --> 00:21:16.750
Theresa, hi.

00:21:18.542 --> 00:21:19.667
Arturo in?

00:21:19.875 --> 00:21:22.125
You're just gonna ask
for my stupid brother?

00:21:22.333 --> 00:21:25.500
You're not gonna tell me where
you've been for the last five months?

00:21:26.542 --> 00:21:28.667
No... Yeah...

00:21:31.167 --> 00:21:33.917
- Who's this?
- Hi. I'm Marissa Cooper.

00:21:34.792 --> 00:21:36.333
So this is your new girlfriend.

00:21:37.917 --> 00:21:40.583
- Oh, so you two were...
- Off and on.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:43.208
We grew up together.
I was the girl next door.

00:21:45.208 --> 00:21:46.750
So am I.

00:21:47.375 --> 00:21:50.500
- Yeah. Arturo?
- Yeah, he's here.

00:21:51.375 --> 00:21:53.208
I'll explain later.

00:22:05.458 --> 00:22:08.667
Mom, look who I found.

00:22:08.875 --> 00:22:10.250
Ryan!

00:22:12.208 --> 00:22:14.958
Where have you been?
I haven't seen your mom in a while.

00:22:15.167 --> 00:22:16.708
Yeah, me neither.

00:22:16.875 --> 00:22:19.708
- And your brother?
- That's kind of why I'm here.

00:22:19.875 --> 00:22:22.375
- So you're here for the car?
- Hey, man.

00:22:23.333 --> 00:22:26.292
- Hey, man, how you been?
- This is Marissa.

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:27.708
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:22:27.917 --> 00:22:29.708
His girlfriend.

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:33.917
Come on, man, let's go. Might take us
a minute to get the engine going.

00:22:34.125 --> 00:22:37.083
- You wanna come?
- You go. I'll hang out here.

00:22:41.667 --> 00:22:44.083
- You could help us cook.
- Great.

00:22:44.292 --> 00:22:48.417
Mom, don't ask her to help. I'm sure she
doesn't cook. She's got maids for that.

00:22:52.917 --> 00:22:54.917
- I don't know where she is.
- So you lost her.

00:22:55.125 --> 00:22:57.583
She's supposed to be at your house.
You lost her.

00:22:57.792 --> 00:23:00.333
Third and long. Big play.

00:23:04.958 --> 00:23:06.208
- They can't stay.
- I know.

00:23:06.417 --> 00:23:10.167
Julie's gonna blow our Jimmy/Rachel
thing. All our hard work for nothing.

00:23:10.375 --> 00:23:15.417
- Who does he think he is?
- Oh, you leaving? It was good to see you.

00:23:15.625 --> 00:23:18.042
- Hey, Seth.
- Hey there, Gramps. Remember Anna?

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:20.708
- How could I forget?
- All right.

00:23:22.917 --> 00:23:26.958
Kiki, I know you're upset with me.
Perhaps we should talk.

00:23:27.125 --> 00:23:31.375
It's okay, Dad. I'm not upset
with you anymore. No talk needed.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.458
Not so fast.

00:23:33.625 --> 00:23:36.375
You own the Heights, right?
The property above the wetlands?

00:23:36.583 --> 00:23:38.125
- Not you too.
- I was wondering...

00:23:38.292 --> 00:23:40.792
...how do you feel about
building a development...

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:43.417
...that only pollutes and destroys
hallowed ground?

00:23:43.625 --> 00:23:46.292
Oh, that's quite a message
you're sending the youth.

00:23:46.458 --> 00:23:50.583
Has she read my report? Is she aware
of the estuary we're building?

00:23:50.750 --> 00:23:52.708
Everybody knows
that doesn't go far enough.

00:23:52.917 --> 00:23:56.208
- It's a Band-Aid for a bullet wound.
- Oh, really?

00:23:56.417 --> 00:23:58.625
Tell you what, I'll get that.

00:24:01.833 --> 00:24:05.083
Summer. Hi. What are you doing here?

00:24:05.292 --> 00:24:08.750
I'm trying to have Thanksgiving. I was
supposed to meet Marissa at her house.

00:24:08.958 --> 00:24:10.875
There was no way
I was eating with my stepmom.

00:24:11.083 --> 00:24:13.083
Why does she need tryptophan?
She's on Valium.

00:24:13.292 --> 00:24:17.417
Oh, yeah. Well, some of the Coopers are
here, but I don't know where Marissa is.

00:24:17.625 --> 00:24:20.167
Well, while I'm here,
maybe we should talk.

00:24:20.375 --> 00:24:25.417
- Yes. What should we talk about?
- About what didn't happen on the yacht.

00:24:25.625 --> 00:24:28.708
So are you gonna invite me in?

00:24:28.917 --> 00:24:32.708
Know what? Let's discuss this in the
pool house. That's gonna work for me.

00:24:32.917 --> 00:24:34.292
Also, let's go around front...

00:24:34.458 --> 00:24:38.000
...because we put some new gardenias in,
and I think you'll be impressed.

00:24:41.500 --> 00:24:45.542
That's weird, because they said those
gardenias should have been in bloom...

00:24:50.417 --> 00:24:52.083
Hey, what's going on?

00:24:52.292 --> 00:24:55.417
I just can't help it.
And I certainly can't explain it.

00:24:55.625 --> 00:24:57.333
- You didn't tell anyone?
- No.

00:24:57.542 --> 00:25:00.000
- Because I'll kill you.
- No, I believe you.

00:25:03.833 --> 00:25:08.250
Could you wait one second? I've got some
green beans I really need to go check on.

00:25:08.458 --> 00:25:11.042
You're passing me up for beans.

00:25:12.292 --> 00:25:13.875
No.

00:25:21.208 --> 00:25:22.792
Is this Ryan?

00:25:23.542 --> 00:25:24.750
You mean Snoopy?

00:25:24.958 --> 00:25:28.583
That's from the eighth-grade musical.
You're a Good Man, Charlie Brown.

00:25:28.792 --> 00:25:31.083
Theresa was Peppermint Patty.

00:25:31.292 --> 00:25:34.625
- And Ryan was Snoopy.
- He was so talented.

00:25:34.833 --> 00:25:38.625
- Ryan did musicals?
- He quit when we got to high school.

00:25:40.375 --> 00:25:42.417
That's a really pretty dress.

00:25:42.625 --> 00:25:46.333
Yeah, that's when me and Ryan
went to the winter dance last year.

00:25:46.542 --> 00:25:49.667
That was a crazy night.
We used to get in all kinds of trouble.

00:25:55.625 --> 00:25:58.458
He just left. You know that?

00:25:59.250 --> 00:26:02.750
He was there one day
and next day his house was empty.

00:26:02.958 --> 00:26:05.875
- I don't think he planned any of it.
- He could have called.

00:26:07.042 --> 00:26:10.500
You know someone your whole life,
you grow up next to them.

00:26:10.833 --> 00:26:13.042
I guess I didn't know him at all.

00:26:18.958 --> 00:26:21.875
This car's hot, man.
Gattas will be psyched.

00:26:22.083 --> 00:26:24.750
Your brother must owe him
a lot of money.

00:26:24.958 --> 00:26:27.792
- That dude's crazier than your brother is.
- Yeah.

00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:31.708
So why are you back here
doing Trey's bitch work?

00:26:31.917 --> 00:26:34.792
Look, Trey was my best friend.
But the guy's trouble.

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:37.000
I've noticed.

00:26:39.292 --> 00:26:41.208
You don't have to do this.

00:26:41.417 --> 00:26:45.042
You could just go back to your new life.
What's Trey gonna do?

00:26:46.083 --> 00:26:48.417
Let's just get this thing running.

00:26:56.875 --> 00:26:59.542
You've been trying to get him
to Thanksgiving for years.

00:26:59.708 --> 00:27:01.167
The only reason why he is here...

00:27:01.375 --> 00:27:04.583
...is because his food didn't show up
and the game is on.

00:27:04.792 --> 00:27:08.042
Slow down with that.
You're drinking on an empty stomach.

00:27:08.250 --> 00:27:10.750
Don't tell me to slow down.
Tell him to hit the bricks.

00:27:10.958 --> 00:27:13.917
- Hit the bricks? Who talks like that?
- Don't judge me.

00:27:14.125 --> 00:27:16.792
I have a family that won't let me cook
for Thanksgiving...

00:27:16.958 --> 00:27:21.000
...my father's using me for my
candied yams, and we are out of merlot!

00:27:21.208 --> 00:27:23.958
Do you want some privacy?

00:27:25.708 --> 00:27:27.750
I'll just...

00:27:34.458 --> 00:27:37.292
- Hey.
- Anna! Why, hello there.

00:27:37.458 --> 00:27:39.417
Where you been?

00:27:39.625 --> 00:27:41.875
Ryan asked me to feed
his sea-monkeys.

00:27:42.083 --> 00:27:45.167
Ryan has sea-monkeys?
I love those things!

00:27:45.375 --> 00:27:48.750
You know what, though? You can't
see them, because they're dead.

00:27:48.958 --> 00:27:51.833
Yeah, suicide. You know
how hard the holidays can be.

00:27:52.875 --> 00:27:54.667
Well...

00:27:55.625 --> 00:27:57.417
...the pool house is empty.

00:27:57.625 --> 00:28:00.625
Maybe we could take
some alone time to hang out.

00:28:00.833 --> 00:28:05.042
- Yeah, let's do that in my room.
- Even better.

00:28:05.208 --> 00:28:06.583
All right!

00:28:15.625 --> 00:28:17.083
So.

00:28:18.625 --> 00:28:20.875
This is your bedroom?

00:28:21.083 --> 00:28:22.833
Yes. Yes, it is.

00:28:28.542 --> 00:28:31.500
Have you met Captain Oats yet?
I don't think you have.

00:28:36.667 --> 00:28:38.500
Seth...

00:28:39.292 --> 00:28:42.958
...you didn't bring me here
to introduce me to Captain Oats.

00:28:43.708 --> 00:28:45.000
No, I didn't.

00:28:46.458 --> 00:28:49.125
That's what I thought.

00:28:58.708 --> 00:29:02.000
I have cauliflower steaming.

00:29:02.208 --> 00:29:06.417
So I'll leave you here
with Captain Oats and I'll be right back.

00:29:13.792 --> 00:29:16.042
So the car's ready to go.

00:29:20.667 --> 00:29:22.250
- Hello?
- Man, it's me. Listen.

00:29:22.708 --> 00:29:25.792
Now, despite what the Penthouse letters
might suggest...

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:29.458
...two girls and one guy...
No, it's not really all it's cracked up to be.

00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:31.042
I know what you mean.

00:29:31.208 --> 00:29:33.417
Can I call you back
when Marissa and I are on the road?

00:29:33.625 --> 00:29:35.958
- Marissa's with you?
- Yeah, why?

00:29:36.167 --> 00:29:39.292
Her mom 's here looking for her.
Call me back, okay?

00:29:39.500 --> 00:29:40.875
Yeah.

00:29:49.333 --> 00:29:52.542
- So Marissa's with Ryan.
- What?

00:29:52.750 --> 00:29:56.042
- I said, Marissa's in Chino.
- I can't hear you.

00:29:56.250 --> 00:30:00.042
I said, Marissa is in Chino!
Wow, that actually happens in real life.

00:30:00.250 --> 00:30:04.125
- What did you say?
- Yeah, no, I said Marissa has my chinos.

00:30:04.333 --> 00:30:07.667
- I love those pants.
- Looks like we'll be here a while.

00:30:07.875 --> 00:30:10.833
- You ready to talk?
- Fresh margs?

00:30:14.042 --> 00:30:16.250
So I'll see you again.

00:30:18.375 --> 00:30:20.833
- Good luck.
- Yeah. You too.

00:30:21.042 --> 00:30:22.625
And, you know...

00:30:24.042 --> 00:30:25.417
...sorry.

00:30:26.750 --> 00:30:28.917
Me too.

00:30:29.125 --> 00:30:32.333
This place isn't as fun as it used to be.

00:30:43.708 --> 00:30:46.625
So how come you didn't tell me
there was a Theresa?

00:30:46.833 --> 00:30:49.583
How come you didn't tell me
about your mom?

00:30:50.917 --> 00:30:54.250
- You're gonna put this on me too?
- I didn't put anything on you.

00:30:54.458 --> 00:30:57.833
- Who do you think she's gonna blame?
- I'll explain it to her.

00:30:58.042 --> 00:31:00.417
- I shouldn't have brought you.
- You're not doing it alone.

00:31:00.625 --> 00:31:03.958
Because you're my wheelman now?
Go back to Newport, I'll take a bus.

00:31:04.167 --> 00:31:06.917
- Ryan!
- This is not a conversation.

00:31:07.125 --> 00:31:09.042
You lied to me.

00:31:27.375 --> 00:31:30.250
What is up with this shirt, Cohen?
Is it, like, childproof?

00:31:30.458 --> 00:31:31.833
Well...

00:31:32.333 --> 00:31:33.833
...why don't you let me do it.

00:31:34.042 --> 00:31:36.625
Oh, way to take charge, Cohen.

00:31:41.875 --> 00:31:45.417
- What? Do I have lipstick on my mouth?
- No.

00:31:45.625 --> 00:31:47.292
No.

00:31:50.333 --> 00:31:51.958
What?

00:31:55.958 --> 00:31:58.000
This is happening.

00:32:02.708 --> 00:32:06.333
Wait. What do you mean,
this is happening?

00:32:06.542 --> 00:32:07.958
No, no, no, Cohen!

00:32:09.708 --> 00:32:12.375
You know what?
This can't be happening.

00:32:12.542 --> 00:32:16.000
Yes, it can. It just was.
I was just expressing awe and delight...

00:32:16.208 --> 00:32:19.042
...which now will be replaced
with a severe bruise on my ass.

00:32:19.250 --> 00:32:22.500
I need to think or eat something.
I feel lightheaded. Can we go inside?

00:32:22.708 --> 00:32:25.958
No, actually, I think that it's best, then...

00:32:26.167 --> 00:32:31.792
...if I go inside, because I'm the host,
and I bring food to you, the guest.

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:36.167
Also, my mom's cooking and that's
something that nobody should witness.

00:32:36.375 --> 00:32:39.667
Plus, my dad is wearing an apron.
Same category.

00:32:39.875 --> 00:32:44.000
And my grandpa's talking politics,
and nobody likes politics.

00:32:44.208 --> 00:32:48.458
And it's very tense, so stay here
where the relaxation is. I'll be back.

00:32:53.042 --> 00:32:55.208
This is your fault.
You let her go with Ryan.

00:32:55.417 --> 00:32:58.417
- I had no idea she was doing this.
- Well, that's encouraging.

00:32:58.625 --> 00:33:01.917
- What sort of father are you?
- You're not serious.

00:33:02.125 --> 00:33:04.500
I may be a lot of things,
but never a bad parent.

00:33:04.708 --> 00:33:06.833
- Destroyer of the environment.
- Tyrannical land baron.

00:33:07.042 --> 00:33:09.417
Stay out of this.
I don't even know what you're doing here.

00:33:09.625 --> 00:33:11.667
Oh, she's our guest. Unlike some people.

00:33:11.875 --> 00:33:14.542
Oh, so suddenly you have standards
about who comes here.

00:33:14.750 --> 00:33:16.917
- What does that mean?
- She wouldn't be in Chino...

00:33:17.125 --> 00:33:18.167
...if she hadn't met him.

00:33:18.375 --> 00:33:21.667
- Ryan's not the problem.
- It's the tree-hugger that brought him in.

00:33:21.875 --> 00:33:25.042
Or the irresponsible parent
trying to get laid on Thanksgiving.

00:33:25.250 --> 00:33:27.167
Excuse me for making up for lost time.

00:33:27.375 --> 00:33:29.667
- Excuse me?
- Sorry, heat of passion.

00:33:29.875 --> 00:33:31.958
Don't expect that to happen very often.

00:33:32.167 --> 00:33:35.667
- People, please. Feel free to share.
- Does anyone want another drink?

00:33:35.875 --> 00:33:38.417
- Seth! Run out to the pool house...
- Can't talk, gotta go.

00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:51.583
Hey, Anna. What's up?

00:33:51.792 --> 00:33:54.125
I'm beating Captain Oats at Jenga.

00:33:55.042 --> 00:34:00.375
I think it's his lack of opposable thumbs
that give me a certain advantage.

00:34:00.542 --> 00:34:02.958
It's getting a little weird in here.

00:34:03.167 --> 00:34:08.000
Well, you left me alone for so long,
I guess I was going a little crazy.

00:34:10.667 --> 00:34:13.542
Captain Oats is a sore loser anyway.

00:34:15.125 --> 00:34:18.583
Have I mentioned that
Thanksgiving is my favorite holiday?

00:34:18.792 --> 00:34:20.750
Well, it is.

00:34:22.042 --> 00:34:24.333
Aren't you kind of hot in this?

00:34:25.125 --> 00:34:27.292
Yes, it is rather balmy.

00:34:28.167 --> 00:34:31.083
- Why don't you take it off.
- Why don't we?

00:34:31.292 --> 00:34:34.167
I was never a fan of it.
My mom picked it out, I was like...

00:34:36.875 --> 00:34:39.542
I mean, wait, that's not true.
I dress myself.

00:34:39.708 --> 00:34:42.167
- I got it.
- Pull on this side...

00:34:42.375 --> 00:34:45.667
- Don't worry, I got it.
- But that's where my head...

00:34:47.375 --> 00:34:49.833
- Seth?
- Okay, that's two bruises today.

00:34:50.042 --> 00:34:51.375
Two?

00:34:51.583 --> 00:34:54.375
Yeah, the first one was from cooking.

00:34:55.958 --> 00:34:59.167
Sweet potatoes just aren't
as sweet as they used to be.

00:34:59.375 --> 00:35:02.875
Speaking of which, I've left them
unattended. I'll be right back.

00:35:03.083 --> 00:35:05.917
What was that, Captain Oats?
He wants a rematch. Do that.

00:35:08.792 --> 00:35:10.958
Do you want a rematch?

00:35:14.375 --> 00:35:16.333
Back so soon? Because I was just...

00:35:19.333 --> 00:35:23.333
I mean, not...
You're very attractive. For a dad.

00:35:23.542 --> 00:35:27.167
Distinguished, but...
Oh, my God.

00:35:51.917 --> 00:35:53.542
You Ryan?

00:35:55.083 --> 00:35:57.792
This is a hot ride, I'll tell you that.

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:00.292
Hard to believe
your brother could pull it off...

00:36:00.500 --> 00:36:04.083
...because he's such
a stupid son of a bitch.

00:36:05.167 --> 00:36:08.833
- Yeah, well, what do you think?
- What, huh? What do I think about what?

00:36:09.042 --> 00:36:12.667
- You take the car, Trey's off the hook.
- Is that the deal?

00:36:12.875 --> 00:36:16.625
- That's what he told me.
- You fellas hear that?

00:36:17.875 --> 00:36:21.292
I been waiting six months for this,
and there's something called interest.

00:36:21.500 --> 00:36:24.917
- I don't have anything.
- Well, interest needs to be paid! All right?

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.667
Get him! Get him!

00:36:31.875 --> 00:36:33.292
Go!

00:36:34.250 --> 00:36:37.458
- What the hell are you doing?
- I followed you.

00:36:38.125 --> 00:36:39.333
Good idea.

00:36:41.125 --> 00:36:43.708
The only thing I know about her
is she likes the Cowboys!

00:36:43.917 --> 00:36:46.792
When was the last time we spent
Thanksgiving together?

00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:50.333
- I have my work, you know that.
- And don't act so innocent.

00:36:50.542 --> 00:36:52.792
I know, Dad, but I didn't
plan on this happening.

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:55.792
Look, I get it.
It's a difficult position to be in.

00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:58.667
- Anna's so smart and funny.
- Yes!

00:36:58.875 --> 00:37:01.833
She's adorable. But Summer is...

00:37:02.542 --> 00:37:04.042
- Summer.
- Yeah.

00:37:05.042 --> 00:37:07.708
- You can't lead these girls on.
- No, right, I know.

00:37:07.875 --> 00:37:10.667
Be a man.
Tell Anna you like Summer.

00:37:10.875 --> 00:37:14.708
Right you are. Except, well...

00:37:14.917 --> 00:37:20.625
Okay.
Well, then tell Summer you like Anna.

00:37:20.833 --> 00:37:23.500
Yeah, again, not so sure.

00:37:23.708 --> 00:37:24.875
Something's burning.

00:37:25.083 --> 00:37:28.042
Guys, I hate to interrupt you,
but there's...

00:37:28.250 --> 00:37:30.000
Oh, my God, my turkey.

00:37:32.458 --> 00:37:36.000
- Oh, that is one toasted bird.
- Come on, Mom.

00:37:39.917 --> 00:37:44.792
- Where are the takeout menus?
- Is everything okay?

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:47.667
- Fine. Let me meet you upstairs.
- I heard the smoke alarm.

00:37:47.833 --> 00:37:49.042
- Summer?
- Anna?

00:37:49.250 --> 00:37:51.333
- Seth?
- Seth?

00:37:52.500 --> 00:37:55.667
Holy awkward. This is weird.
I wanna explain everything to you guys...

00:37:55.875 --> 00:37:57.667
- I kissed you.
- I know.

00:37:57.875 --> 00:37:59.833
- I kissed you.
- Also true.

00:38:00.042 --> 00:38:01.792
I always knew
you were a late bloomer.

00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:05.667
- Thanks, Mom. Don't go.
- Oh, you don't want her to go?

00:38:05.875 --> 00:38:08.458
No. I mean yes. I mean yes.

00:38:10.417 --> 00:38:14.042
- Nice.
- That was awkward. Finally she's gone.

00:38:14.250 --> 00:38:18.250
- Let me tell you something, Summer...
- I don't feel very good.

00:38:26.667 --> 00:38:29.167
The car's delivered, the debt's paid.

00:38:29.375 --> 00:38:32.500
But I am never doing anything
for you again, you understand?

00:38:32.708 --> 00:38:35.833
- I'm sorry, man.
- They could've killed me.

00:38:36.042 --> 00:38:39.292
I also know that no one else
would've done this for me.

00:38:40.250 --> 00:38:42.167
But I get it. We're done.

00:38:45.542 --> 00:38:49.167
- Well, I'll come by to see you.
- Don't.

00:38:50.500 --> 00:38:53.042
You've got a chance, little brother.

00:38:53.250 --> 00:38:56.833
You gotta leave me behind.
Leave all this behind.

00:39:00.875 --> 00:39:04.583
- Take care of yourself.
- Yeah.

00:39:05.583 --> 00:39:09.208
Well, you should jet.
You got people waiting for you.

00:39:43.708 --> 00:39:45.375
So that was Chino.

00:39:50.333 --> 00:39:54.875
I guess I never realized that
when you left, you left people behind.

00:39:58.667 --> 00:40:01.375
I never wanna do that again.

00:40:03.625 --> 00:40:04.875
You won't have to...

00:40:06.625 --> 00:40:08.333
...Snoopy.

00:40:50.333 --> 00:40:53.583
So we should watch
a game sometime.

00:40:53.792 --> 00:40:57.667
Yeah, yeah. I'd like...
I don't know if I'm...

00:40:59.458 --> 00:41:01.333
Well, when you're ready.

00:41:01.542 --> 00:41:02.750
Yeah.

00:41:05.375 --> 00:41:07.125
That was good.

00:41:10.208 --> 00:41:12.875
Oh, thank God. Are you okay?

00:41:13.042 --> 00:41:14.833
Yeah, Mom. I'm fine.

00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:19.875
- Why didn't you tell me you were going?
- Julie. It's Thanksgiving.

00:41:21.750 --> 00:41:22.958
Lo mein?

00:41:28.708 --> 00:41:31.167
Hey, man. What are you doing?

00:41:32.333 --> 00:41:36.500
- Not lying with Captain Oats.
- Why are you on the floor?

00:41:36.708 --> 00:41:39.875
I figured I'd just end up here anyway,
so I cut out the middleman.

00:41:40.083 --> 00:41:44.000
- Looks like things went pretty well.
- Yeah, same for you. Nice shiner.

00:41:44.208 --> 00:41:46.208
So can we sit with you and Captain Oats?

00:41:46.583 --> 00:41:48.750
Yeah. Please.

00:41:50.208 --> 00:41:54.167
Hey, nothing says Thanksgiving
like mushu pork. Thanks.

00:41:57.042 --> 00:41:59.333
So, what did your brother say?

00:42:01.750 --> 00:42:03.833
Goodbye.

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:08.667
- So Chino was...
- It's good to be home.

00:42:17.375 --> 00:42:21.000
So, Seth, did you know
that Ryan did musicals?

00:42:22.667 --> 00:42:24.000
That's extremely minty of you.

00:42:24.208 --> 00:42:27.667
I didn't know they had musicals in Chino.
Or dancing or laughter.

00:42:27.875 --> 00:42:32.500
- No one there is as funny as you.
- So we finally agree I'm the funny one.

00:42:32.708 --> 00:42:37.333
Look at that. We all learned some
valuable lessons this Thanksgiving.

00:42:37.542 --> 00:42:39.500
It's heartwarming.
